                },
                "cam": {
                  "mode": "save",
                  "banner": "SAVING CLIP → VAULT"
                },
                "pw": {
                  "value": 120
                },
                "log": {
                  "log": [
                    {
                      "tag": "CAM",
                      "text": "clip 00:14 → vault"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "heading": "Thermal envelope — throttle, shutdown, recover",
        "accent": "amber",
        "source": "https://github.com/doorbuzz-cloud/chime/blob/main/docs/hld.md#thermal",
        "text": [
          "Vision HP's H.264 encoder can outrun its cooling on a hot afternoon. Firmware throttles the encoder at 75 °C and hard-powers the chip off at 95 °C — but the doorbell never leaves the network, because Sentry LP owns the radio and keeps talking while its big sibling cools.",
          "The temperature panel tracks the die across every step against the declared warning and shutdown thresholds; the PIR panel shows the visit that started the load."
        ],
        "bullets": [
          "The PIR cone computes tripped vs clear from geometry — the walk-up stays outside sensor range until step 3",
          "Warning and critical thresholds are declared once on the panel; the engine colors every step from the value alone",
          "Steps 8–9 are the point: the always-on chip narrates the shutdown while the hot chip is completely off"
        ],
        "contract": {
          "title": "On the wire: thermal event (MQTT)",
          "source": "https://github.com/doorbuzz-cloud/chime/blob/main/docs/wire.md#thermal-event",
          "fields": [
            {
              "k": "type",
              "v": "\"thermal_shutdown\"",
              "g": "published by Sentry LP, not the chip that overheated",
              "hot": true
            },
            {
              "k": "chip",
              "v": "\"vision-hp\"",
              "g": "which core powered down"
            },
            {
              "k": "die_c",
              "v": "96.2",
              "g": "last reading before the rail dropped"
            },
            {
              "k": "resume_below_c",
              "v": "60",
              "g": "re-arm threshold; Sentry re-wakes the chip under it"
            }
          ],
          "note": "Pulse turns this into the resident-facing \"camera paused to cool down\" push — the device reports its own outage."
        },
